\ A self-recursive word threads a quotation argument and, on each recursive
\ self-tail-call, replaces it with a fresh literal quotation `[ 42 ]`. At the
\ back-edge that new argument is a quotation_body (a literal), not the threaded
\ input, so the argument copy would read an unwritten slot without reification.
\ The base case returns the carried quotation, which is then called -- proving it
\ survived the back-edges with a valid code_ptr.
acc: ( n q -- q ) [ over 0 > [ swap 1 - swap drop [ 42 ] acc ] [ nip ] if ] ;

2 [ 0 ] acc call .
